# Build-context ignore rules for feishu-bot/Dockerfile.
#
# Docker resolves this file (named after the Dockerfile, sitting next to it) in
# preference to the context-root .dockerignore. It matters here because the
# build context is the REPOSITORY ROOT (the service depends on the sibling
# package im-core/, which a per-service context cannot see), so without these
# rules `docker build -f feishu-bot/Dockerfile .` would upload every dev
# virtualenv, node_modules, and the repo's .git into the context.
#
# Do NOT ignore whole service directories: the Dockerfile COPYs both
# `im-core/` and `feishu-bot/`.

# Python dev artifacts
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Review/inspection scratch space — never ship vendored SDK copies
.sdk-inspect/

# Local env & secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Repo noise that must not enter the image
/tests
*.md
!README.md
